                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone who suffers from triskaidekaphobia."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8fc04e9c-2e0f-4483-8cba-64211d4967a0",
                                "sense_id": "b2bbb72d-c9ed-3673-9336-c43e88d2dbc3",
                                "text": "After reading through Lachenmeyer’s 13: The Story of the World's Most Popular Superstition, I discovered that very few triskaidekaphobes today connect unlucky 13 to the Last Supper, even though this is thought to be the major historical basis for the superstition (Lachenmeyer 132). […] Lachenmeyer gives an example of a typical triskaidekaphobe, a 40-year-old man from Wisconsin who has paranoia regarding Friday the 13ᵗʰ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "802a71b3-c9bf-42c8-a067-23f834fc9571",
                                "sense_id": "b2bbb72d-c9ed-3673-9336-c43e88d2dbc3",
                                "text": "For example, triskaidekaphobes like to point out the fate of the 1970 Apollo 13 lunar mission, blaming its near-disastrous outcome on its number and the time it launched, 13:13 CST."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
